WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.564
This section begins with a summary
of the information that we

00:00:03.604 --> 00:00:06.839
have covered in the past
sections on coping strategies.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.726
We have now covered the essential elements

00:00:08.766 --> 00:00:11.610
of the three main types
of coping strategies.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:15.859
As we discussed in the previous
section, social support coping

00:00:15.899 --> 00:00:20.590
involves seeking problem solving
or stress management help from others.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:27.050
For example, receiving information or advice
about your tinnitus, problem solving,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:33.172
obtaining tangible support such
as compensation, problem solving,

00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:36.766
talking with someone to receive
their emotional support,

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:42.357
stress management, seeking information
about how others relax when

00:00:42.397 --> 00:00:47.430
their tinnitus symptoms are bothering
them, stress management.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.430
Let us run through some examples
of types of coping strategies.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:56.498
Please note that you may find that some
coping strategies do not neatly

00:00:56.538 --> 00:01:01.230
fit into either problem solving or stress
management strategies categories.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.996
We will pause after each one so
you can think about whether it

00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:09.030
is a problem solving strategy
or a stress management strategy.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.370
Then we will give you the answer.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:15.930
Our first example is using
negotiation skills.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.171
This is problem solving coping primarily,

00:01:19.211 --> 00:01:22.951
but stress management as well
because it might help you feel good

00:01:22.991 --> 00:01:26.950
about yourself and better about
the situation that you are facing.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:31.690
Our second example
is getting physical exercise.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.288
Now this could be stress management
coping because exercise definitely

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:40.329
has an enhancing effect on well-being
and emotion, but it could also be

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:44.770
considered a problem solving strategy
if the problem is being overweight.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.730
Our third example is practice meditation.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.811
This is stress management coping,

00:01:51.851 --> 00:01:55.963
but it may help you be better
at problem solving because you will be

00:01:56.003 --> 00:02:00.610
more calm and able to think more
clearly after you finish meditating.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:05.470
Our next example is creating
a plan of action.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:08.430
This is problem solving coping.

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.930
Our next example is talking
to someone else about your feelings.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.630
This is stress management coping.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.810
Our last example is drinking alcohol.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.584
This is stress management
coping because alcohol

00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:30.362
and smoking etc can
temporarily change one's mood,

00:02:30.402 --> 00:02:36.090
but it is not as adaptive and healthy
as other choices like exercise.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.490
We have one last part to go over
to help you cope with tinnitus.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.430
There are four suggestions in this part.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.359
These are a few more tools
to help you get to a more

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:51.030
positive mindset despite
the fact of having tinnitus.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.004
In the earlier section on stress
management coping we talked about

00:02:55.044 --> 00:02:59.830
creating positive experiences as a tool
to deal with unchangeable stress.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.210
Now we shift here into
more internal strength.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:05.670
The first step toward
increasing your personal coping

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.210
effectiveness is to acknowledge
your personal strengths.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.390
We all have some things that we do
well and other things not so well.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.390
It is important to be aware
and own our strengths.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.258
It is also important to be
aware of the positive

00:03:21.298 --> 00:03:25.410
or negative things we say often
privately about ourselves.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:28.644
The ways we talk about ourselves
often become so habitual

00:03:28.684 --> 00:03:32.331
and second nature that we don't
even notice what we're saying.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.074
Think for a moment about
some positive things

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.870
you can say about your personal strengths.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.850
If you immediately think I have none,

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:47.670
take some time to dig deeper and try to answer
the question what are your strengths?

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:53.310
Examples of strengths may include
you make an effort to be on time.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.830
You are able to keep a promise.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.066
You have served your country
by being in the military.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.970
You are dedicated to your job,
your family, or a cause.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:07.017
You listen to people when they
want to tell you their stories.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.127
You are able to be decisive when you're

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:12.370
in complicated situations
that need a quick response.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.150
You make others laugh.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.970
These are examples of strengths.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.430
Please take some time to think
about your own strengths.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.870
We all have them.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.630
You most certainly do.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.183
Otherwise you would not be
sitting in front of a computer

00:04:26.223 --> 00:04:29.399
screen trying to learn
the information in this course.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:35.390
Here are some examples of ways that you
can develop a more positive mindset.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.770
This kind of outlook will help prevent
tinnitus from ruling your life.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:44.330
One, use positive statements
about specific events.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:49.690
For instance, I can finish what I am
doing despite the ringing in my ears.

00:04:49.730 --> 00:04:54.930
Or I can go out with my friends
or buddies even if my tinnitus kicks up.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:59.670
Two, use positive statements
about your efforts.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:05.010
For instance, great, I did it
despite that darn ringing in my ears.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.458
I got through that all right,

00:05:06.498 --> 00:05:09.969
even though my tinnitus would
not stop when I wanted it to.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.620
I really handled that pretty well,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:15.013
even with the tinnitus
interfering with my communication.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.448
Keep in mind that we
often are not conditioned

00:05:18.488 --> 00:05:21.070
to say positive things about ourselves.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:24.330
Instead, we are often tough on ourselves.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.910
We demand that we must be strong
and power through the tough times.

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:34.590
It may be awkward at first to say positive
things to yourself, but give it a try.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:38.214
Remember that the more that you
concentrate on positive things,

00:05:38.254 --> 00:05:42.268
the more you will decrease your often
repetitive focus on your stress,

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:45.630
such as tinnitus, and what
is wrong with your life.
